WEBVTT

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.140
Thank you.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:30.640
You

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:25.920
Have you come with?

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:33.750
Run for it!

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:39.900
They mustn't get away!

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:41.540
Bill, you look after the girls!

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:50.710
They're behind those rocks!

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:58.480
Watch it, Carson!

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.520
Right the way, Morgan, so I can shoot.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:24.440
Good work, Nicole, miss.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:37.570
Thank you.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:18.750
The mystery riders captured him and Kraft and took him to the rock hideout.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:21.260
The mystery riders!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.940
They're on the way to the trading bulls to get you, Johnny.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:43.880
Now is not a chance to rescue Kraft and your father before the riders get back to the hideout.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.800
This fellow's uniform may come in handy.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.610
One man on guard at the entrance.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.670
We don't know how many there may be inside.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:09.540
That's your job.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.000
I can see their camp from the top of that ridge.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.840
I'll go up there and signal you how many men I see.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:42.920
Now, now. Don't you worry. We'll have your father and craft out of there before long.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:48.140
Carson won't leave us in the lurch. He'll find some way to get us out of here.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:55.060
I'm sure, but even though he brings all my men from the trading post, there's bound to be lots of shooting.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.980
Well, you and I stand a pretty good chance of getting hit, maybe killed.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.600
Why, I never thought of that.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:09.220
Why, I wish I'd told Carson where I'd hid the gold, just in case anything should happen to me.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:09.520
Yeah.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.760
Oh, what's the matter, Fargo?

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:15.120
Oh, my old heart's acting up again.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.780
I guess the excitement is too much for an old war horse like me.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:25.380
Well, I'm bothered that way at times myself.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:28.400
I always carry a little heart stimulant with me.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:35.360
Here, drink some of this.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:40.180
Do you think it'll help me?

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.340
Well, it's been a great help to me, more than once.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:26.040
There's a signal.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.330
You're in luck.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.720
It says there's only one other guard inside.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:39.290
Fargo?

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.230
Oh, no.

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:43.530
Oh, it seems to be getting worse.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:46.510
I'm worried, Kraft.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.240
That gold's on my mind.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.730
If anything should happen to me, I...

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:54.070
Well, perhaps you'd better tell me where it's hid.

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.660
That is, if you feel that you can trust me.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.770
Why, of course I trust you, Kraft.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.200
Didn't you save my life?

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.740
If anything could happen to me,

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:12.520
you tell Carson that the gold is in the cave

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.040
at the foot of Iron Mountain,

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:17.820
just beyond the gulch.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.980
You devil!

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.350
Here comes one of the gang, and he's got Fargo's daughter!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.360
Did you meet the boys?

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:02.920
They're looking.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:03.800
Person!

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.420
You've come too late. Fargo.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:33.580
Daddy! Daddy!

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:37.800
Why, I'm sorry, little one, but your daddy's had a bad spell.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.750
I guess they treated him pretty rough.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:51.600
I did all I could for him, but, uh, poor girl.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:54.800
There, there, Johnny.

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.150
He wouldn't want you to grieve, though.

00:10:58.910 --> 00:10:59.970
But he was all I...

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:11.820
name? I'll find the man responsible for this if it's the last thing I do. Have you any idea who he is?

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:19.260
No, but I'll find out. I found where his men go to meet him. Where? In a barn near the trading post.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:23.570
Well, then we have no time to lose. We must get to the trading post at once.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:40.320
I'm sure that Miss Carter will take good care of you did I will do poor child, and I'll make all arrangements for your daddy's burial

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:54.130
Oh, thank you. All right. Let's get busy Carson. Now. Why did you say this barn is there?

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:59.960
My flat back of your store crap my barn a meeting place for

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.430
outlaws? What? This is enough to make you suspect that I'm mixed up in this caution. As a matter of

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:09.860
fact, I have suspected you, Kraft, but I had to change my mind when I saw the Mr. Riders take

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:14.680
you prisoner. Yes, one of my men must be at the bottom of this, and I'll soon find out who he is.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:29.520
Good. We'll scout around the barn and see what we can find. Hurry up.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.400
Block the secret entrance to the barn.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.030
Carson's fooling around there.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:56.680
Carson arrested Kraft and their gun to the trading post.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:57.760
What about Fargo?

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:58.320
He's dead.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:12:59.920
Kraft must be at the bottom.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:29.500
of this back to the trading post quick i saw the outlaws come in here when i followed them in they

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.200
There must be a secret exit. We've got to find it.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:42.860
Here! Mystery ride!

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:12.810
Four of you come with me.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:17.400
Wade, you watch the barn in case Crash should try to escape through the secret exit.

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:36.760
Don't make a sound.

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:40.700
Wade, you.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:41.860
Do you know him?

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:44.440
He was with my pack train when the government door was stolen.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.640
He's going to tell me who the real leader of the gang is.

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:48.690
Try and make me.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:51.330
The boys know I'm in here, and they'll come looking for me.

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.130
By that time, you'll be through talking.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:54.510
Get that rope.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:55.740
Well, Carson, you wouldn't...

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.660
Yes, I would, unless you tell me what I want to know.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:00.590
Keep him covered.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:18.880
Excitement, boys.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:20.540
Don't try to buff, Kraft.

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:21.970
We've come for you.

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:23.840
This is your finish.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:27.720
You're wrong, Reynolds.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:29.340
It's your finish.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.220
Well, you're not smart enough to lead men like these.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.740
I was smart enough to turn them against you.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:38.480
And that's exactly why they've got to get rid of you now.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:42.760
That is, if they expect to share in Fargo's gold.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.530
You mean, you found out where the gold is, Chief?

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:51.720
Exactly. I'm the only man alive that can lead you to it.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.120
Grab hold of him, boys.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:54.820
We know how to make him talk, don't we?

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:03.240
Why, the boys don't have to make me talk.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.330
I'm glad to show them where the gold is.

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:16.330
All they've got to do is to choose between you and me.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:20.080
What have you got to offer the boys, Reynolds?

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.680
I've got a secret worth a half a million dollars.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:31.780
You can't get away with this crap.

00:16:32.588 --> 00:16:34.388
The men outside are still with me.

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:51.520
Well, come on, speak up.

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:54.440
Like that, he'd kill me if I told him.

00:16:54.732 --> 00:16:55.492
He'll never know.

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:56.660
I promise you that.

00:16:57.708 --> 00:16:58.988
But if you don't speak up,

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:02.540
Men coming.

00:17:03.548 --> 00:17:04.508
Over there by that dog.
